  "thought": "Now I understand `parse_amount`: it returns an int in cents, raises ValueError for empty strings or invalid formats, and can return negative values. My `journal_imbalance` function must: 1) Raise ValueError if `lines` is empty. 2) Raise ValueError if any account is empty. 3) Treat empty debit/credit strings as 0 (since `parse_amount` raises on empty). 4) Raise ValueError if `parse_amount` raises (invalid format). 5) Raise ValueError if any parsed amount is negative. 6) Return sum(debits) - sum(credits). I also need to check the design review notes from @eng-87. Let me message them first, then implement.",
